        "original_id": "f23552f6-eae8-5ac0-9817-38b8f6e5f271",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Pennsylvania Route 380\n- Places: Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania\n- Products: Interstate 579, PPG Paints Arena\n- Organizations: Pittsburgh Penguins, National Hockey League, Pittsburgh Power, Arena Football League\n\nFacts:\n- Pennsylvania Route 380 is officially designated SR 400 because Interstate 380 exists elsewhere in Pennsylvania.\n- Pennsylvania Route 380 is also known as the J.F. Bonetto Memorial Highway and, within Pittsburgh, as Bigelow Boulevard, Baum Boulevard, and Frankstown Road.\n- Pennsylvania Route 380 is a 32.80-mile state highway in western Pennsylvania.\n- The western terminus of Pennsylvania Route 380 is at Interstate 579 in downtown Pittsburgh near PPG Paints Arena.\n- PPG Paints Arena is a multi-purpose indoor arena in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania.\n- From 2011 to 2014, PPG Paints Arena was the home of the Pittsburgh Power of the Arena Football League.\n- PPG Paints Arena serves as the home of the Pittsburgh Penguins of the National Hockey League.",
